# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. This file is not — never put a real key in here.
# Check your setup at any time with:  uv run fernpost doctor

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model access. You need ONE of the two options below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Option A (recommended). One key reaches every provider, so the three-model
# comparison works without signing up to three vendors.
#   1. Sign up at https://logfire.pydantic.dev
#   2. Activate the gateway in your organization settings
#   3. Create a Gateway API key
PYDANTIC_AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Option B. Bring your own provider keys. Set whichever you have, then pass a
# direct model string, e.g. --model anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5
# You only need the provider for the model you actually run.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tracing. Optional, but this is where the experiment gets interesting.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Without this, runs work normally and Pydantic AI is still instrumented
# locally, so the trace-based evaluators keep working. With it, every run and
# every evaluation result is sent to Logfire and stays linked to the trace that
# produced it. Same signup as the gateway above.
LOGFIRE_TOKEN=
